*
* START-HISTORY:
* 18 Oct 26 Windows port - from Linux 3bca321 (12 Oct 26): New.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $sl_sgr(code, seq)
*
*     code  a style code from $sl_attr: n normal, r reverse, u underline, x reverse and underline
*     seq   returned: the terminal's own strings (SD's @(-13) and friends, so terminfo decides),
*           first switching both off and then the ones the code needs, so the result does not
*           depend on what the terminal was doing before.  An unknown code gives n's.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine sl_sgr(code, seq)
$catalog $sl_sgr

   begin case
      case code = 'r' ; seq = @(-16) : @(-13)
      case code = 'u' ; seq = @(-14) : @(-15)
      case code = 'x' ; seq = @(-13) : @(-15)
      case 1 ; seq = @(-14) : @(-16)
   end case

   return
end

* END-CODE
